indexed scope lookups using typed edges and walkers.

Models the core entities from issue #491:
  - Project owns content
  - Folder/File live under a project, with a direct access_scope_id
  - AccessScope is the permission boundary (PROJECT or FOLDER kind)
  - AccessGrant binds a principal (User or Project) to a scope with a role

Two walkers demonstrate the contrast:
  - LegacyAccessWalker: hand-rolled recursion through parent edges, the very
    pain the issue describes.
  - ScopeAccessWalker: indexed lookup using owner_project_id / access_scope_id,
    the proposed fix.
"""

node Item {
    has title: str = "";
    has owner_project_id: int = 0;
    has access_scope_id: int = 0;
}

node Folder(Item) {
    has folder_id: int = 0;
