"""GEDCOM-style typed record graph: lazy pointer resolution + safety net for unknown substructures.

Models the essential shape of the magicsunday/gedcom-parser full-typed-model goal:
- Records (individual, source) as node archetypes with typed `has` fields.
- Pointer references between records as typed edges carrying the xref payload.
- Substructure containers as edges with optional payload, plus a safety-net
  `RawSubstructure` edge to preserve unmodeled tags (the issue's
  "$unknown" requirement) so nothing is silently lost.
- A walker that traverses the record graph following pointer edges, walking
  the same chain the issue describes
  (`$document->individuals[i]->bapm[0]->plac->sour[0]->source($document)->…`)
  and accumulates visited records into a single typed `report`, with an
  explicit cycle guard (jac 0.36.1 walkers have no built-in dedup).
"""

# --- Value objects: hand-written leaf payloads (DATE / PLAC / AGE analog) ---
node DateValue { has raw: str = ""; }
node PlaceValue { has raw: str = ""; }
node AgeValue { has years: int = 0; }

# --- Record archetypes: full-typed model classes (generated in the real repo) ---
node Individual {
    has name: str = "";
    has sex: str = "";
    has bapm_place: str = "";
    has bapm_date: str = "";
}

node SourceRecord {
    has title: str = "";
    has author: str = "";
}

# --- Pointer payload: lazy resolution keeps the xref, never cycles ---
edge Pointer {
    has xref: str = "";
}

# --- Substructure container edges (one per GEDCOM substructure) ---
edge BapmEvent { }            # baptism event substructure
edge Citation { has page: str = ""; }   # sour citation under plac
edge RawSubstructure {       # safety net: any tag the typed model does not consume
