"""Maven transitive dependency repository resolution.

Models the core pain from MNG-6397: a project declares a single allowed
repository, but a deep chain of transitive pom inheritance drags in
parent poms that carry *other* repository definitions. A resolver that
walks the dependency + parent chain blindly ends up referencing
forbidden mirrors (e.g. spring-milestone).

Archetypes:
    Repository  -- a maven repository (id, url, kind).
    Artifact    -- a coordinate (groupId:artifactId:type:version).
    Pom         -- a pom node; declares dependencies + parent + repositories.
    Build       -- the user's project root (the spawn site).

Edges (typed, semantic):
    DependsOn    -- pom -> artifact (runtime/build dependency).
    ParentPom    -- pom -> parent pom (inheritance link; the chain that
                    smuggles rogue repos down into the build).
    DeclaresRepo -- pom -> repository (a repo a pom defines).
    Allows       -- build -> repository (the *only* repo the user permits).

Walker:
    RepoAuditor  -- spawn on a Build, walks DependsOn -> Pom, follows
