"""Family Genealogy Graph: evidence-backed ancestry and kinship research.

Models PERSON, KINSHIP_RELATIONSHIP, NAME_VARIANT, EVIDENCE, RESEARCH_TASK
as node archetypes. Relationships are typed edges carrying confidence and
source backing. A PedigreeWalker traverses ancestry chains, a ResearchPlanner
walks the graph collecting unresolved candidates and proposes follow-up
tasks, and an InvalidationWalker cascades a "disputed" flag through evidence
chains so downstream nodes can react. Cycle policy is explicit because Jac
0.36.1 walkers have no built-in once-per-node visit set.
