number of hops grows. We represent a small cross-subsidiary ownership graph
as typed nodes/edges, then walk it with two traversal strategies:

  * VectorRetriever  — a flat, single-hop lookup walker (simulates vector RAG).
  * KnowledgeGraphWalker — a typed-edge multi-hop walker that traverses
    subsidiary -> parent ownership links and accumulates facts along the way.

A CycleGuard walker demonstrates the confounder from the issue: a conglomerate
whose ownership structure forms a cycle would hang a naive walker; we use an
explicit guard set to make the policy observable.
