A maintainer on the project patrickkelley/gosuspoon (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #30: GosuEnvironment.scanTypeNames lacks symlink cycle detection leading to StackOverflowError

## Summary
`GosuEnvironment.scanTypeNames` recursively calls `collect(File root, File dir, List<String> out)`. For each entry in `dir.listFiles()`, it checks `f.isDirectory()` and unconditionally recurses into `collect(root, f, out)`. Because `File.isDirectory()` resolves and follows symbolic links, any symlink pointing to an ancestor or enclosing directory creates an infinite directory recursion, resulting in a `StackOverflowError`.

## Location
- `spoon-gosu/src/main/java/spoon/gosu/GosuEnvironment.java:114-126`
```java
private static void collect(File root, File dir, List<String> out) {
    File[] files = dir.listFiles();
    if (files == null) {
        return;
    }
    for (File f : files) {
        if (f.isDirectory()) {
            collect(root, f, out);
        } else if (f.getName().endsWith(".gs") || f.getName().endsWith(".gsx")) {
            out.add(fullyQualifiedName(root, f));
        }
    }
}
```

## Reproduction
```bash
mkdir -p /tmp/cycle-demo/sub
ln -s /tmp/cycle-demo /tmp/cycle-demo/sub/loop
```
Calling `GosuEnvironment.initialize(List.of(new File("/tmp/cycle-demo"))).scanTypeNames(...)` enters unbounded recursion across `/tmp/cycle-demo/sub/loop/sub/loop/...` until `java.lang.StackOverflowError`.

## Impact
Projects containing circular directory symlinks, recursive build directories, or IDE link structures crash Spoon during startup before parsing begins.

## Suggested fix
Track canonical or real paths using a visited `Set<Path>` or use `Files.walkFileTree` with a loop/cycle detector:
```java
Path realPath = f.toPath().toRealPath();
if (visited.add(realPath)) {
    collect(root, f, out, visited);
}
```

